    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1058">

                <pb facs="1332" n="1322" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.48/6–1847: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-25T19:00:00-04:00">June 25, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>775. Definite authorization re negotiation relief agreement can be sent quickly
                    (Reurtel 1324 June 18 repeated Shanghai 548) upon receipt of reply to Deptel 738
                    June 17. Proposed text of relief agreement being negotiated with Italy being
                    sent in immediately following cable<anchor n="46" xml:id="d1058-f1"/> based
                    largely on terms of relief Act. Ur comments and suggestions for modification to
                    meet situation in China are desired. Sent Nanking as Depts 775 repeated to
                    Shanghai as Depts 1060.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1058-f1" n="46" xml:id="d1058-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 776, June 25, 7 p.m., not printed; for text of agreement between the
                    United States and Italy regarding relief assistance, signed at Rome on July 4,
                    1947, see Department of State Treaties and Other International Acts Series No.
                    1653, or 61 Stat. (pt. 3) 3135.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
